{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.PairwiseInteractionDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.PairwiseInteractionDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.pairwise_interaction_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.pairwise_interaction_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L250-L274","doc":"**Pairwise decomposition of a braided interaction.**  Three claims:\n\n1. a composite interaction *reduces* to pairwise ones (hexagon);\n2. that reduction is *independent of the route taken* (Yang–Baxter);\n3. a word bringing every one of the `C(n,2)` strand pairs into contact\n   costs at least `C(n,2)` elementary crossings.\n\nParts 1 and 2 say the many-body content of an interaction lives in the\n*sequence* of pairwise crossings rather than in an irreducible many-body\nvertex.  Part 3 says that sequence is not free. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:pairwise-interaction-decomposition","label":"prop:pairwise-interaction-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.three_crossings_needed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.three_crossings_needed","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L236-L242","doc":"The three-strand instance: a fully interacting triple costs three\ncrossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.card_allPairs_le_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.card_allPairs_le_length","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L224-L234","doc":"**Every pair must be paid for.**  A word in elementary crossings whose net\npermutation reverses *every* strand pair has length at least `C(n,2)`.\n\nFor three strands this is three crossings.  Two will not do: after two\nelementary crossings one of the three pairs has never been adjacent.  A\nthree-body interaction is not two two-body interactions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.card_crossedPairs_le_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.card_crossedPairs_le_length","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L214-L222","doc":"**A word brings no more pairs into contact than it has letters.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.crossedPairs_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.crossedPairs_one","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L209-L212","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.braidWordPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.braidWordPerm","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L203-L207","doc":"The permutation of strand positions realised by a word in elementary\ncrossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.card_crossedPairs_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.card_crossedPairs_step","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L176-L201","doc":"**One elementary crossing brings at most one new pair into contact.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.crossedPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.crossedPairs","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L171-L174","doc":"The strand pairs whose order `σ` reverses.  Two strands have interacted\nexactly when their order is reversed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.card_allPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.card_allPairs","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L157-L169","doc":"There are exactly `C(n,2)` strand pairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.allPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.allPairs","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L153-L155","doc":"All `C(n,2)` strand pairs `i < j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.eq_of_reverses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.eq_of_reverses","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L103-L149","doc":"**An elementary crossing can newly reverse only the pair it acts on.**\nIf `u < v` but the crossing puts them in the opposite order, then `u` and\n`v` are precisely the two exchanged positions.\n\nThis is the whole content of the counting bound: a crossing is a *local*\nevent, so it cannot bring an arbitrary pair of strands into contact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.perm","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L100-L101","doc":"The permutation realised by an elementary crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.lo_ne_hi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.lo_ne_hi","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L97-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.adj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.adj","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The two positions are adjacent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.hi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.hi","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The upper of the two exchanged positions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.lo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.lo","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The lower of the two exchanged positions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.AdjSwap","kind":"structure","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L83-L91","doc":"An elementary crossing exchanges two strand positions adjacent in the\norder.  There are `n - 1` of these, the Artin generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.triple_crossing_route_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.triple_crossing_route_independent","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L61-L71","doc":"**Route independence (Yang–Baxter, Reidemeister III).**  A degenerate\ntriple crossing has two perturbations into a triangle of three pairwise\ncrossings — slide the third strand above, or below.  The two sequences\nare equal, so the decomposition into pairwise events is well defined\neven though the order of the events is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.composite_crossing_eq_two_elementary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.composite_crossing_eq_two_elementary","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/pairwise-interaction-decomposition.lean#L47-L57","doc":"**Composite reduction.**  Passing the composite system `X ⊗ Y` past `Z`\nis not a new ternary operation: it is the elementary crossing of `Y` past\n`Z` followed by the elementary crossing of `X` past `Z`, reassociated.\n\nIn a strict monoidal category the associators drop out and the statement\nreads `c_{X⊗Y, Z} = (c_{X,Z} ⊗ id_Y) ∘ (id_X ⊗ c_{Y,Z})`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}